{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Issachar.</b> It has two shins — one for the meaning of ״נתן אלהים את שכרי,״ and one corresponding to ״שכר שכרתיך,״ which is a term of disgrace, and therefore it is not read [i.e., the name is not pronounced as given]. Another explanation: for this reason it is not read [as written] — because she was given to Job his son, as it is written: ״ובני יששכר וגו׳.״ Issachar said: ״Job is not a fitting name; I will add one letter from my name to him and call his name Yashuv,״ and that is what is written in the portion of Pinchas: לישוב."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The note appears to cite Genesis 46:13 (״ובני יששכר״) where Job appears in the list of Issachar's sons; 'אינה נקראת' likely means the defective/doubled shin form is not read as written. The midrashic identification of Job (איוב/יוב) as Issachar's son and the letter play between יששכר and ישוב are preserved literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:22.215081419Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}